{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nOn current `origin/main`, `infra/terraform-github/versions.tf` describes the Terraform provider path as equivalent to the shell fallback. They intentionally differ: `terraform-github/main.tf` locks only `main` so release tags remain available, while `apply-mirror-lock.sh` locks `main` and all tags. The comment hides a security/operations tradeoff.\n\n## Approach\nReplace the parity claim with a concise statement of the intentional tag-protection difference and point to the authoritative implementations.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The comment accurately distinguishes main-only Terraform locking from shell main-and-tag locking.\n- [x] No Terraform value or executable behavior changes.\n- [x] Terraform format/validate and `make lint` pass."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788762785908405001,"uuid":"019f4ae4-d27a-467b-8d2c-c7a88e75e4ef"}